{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/917294-changelings-sorcery","id":917294,"title":"Changelings & Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-19T05:11:37-07:00","id":917294,"title":"Changelings & Sorcery","content":"Hello fair folk,<br /> <br /> I would like to know your ideas about the sorcery and changelings. Are changelings capable of doing sorcery, are there any connections between sorcery and arts? Realm system makes changeling magic much more dynamic then sorcery, but arts are just as static as sorcery without realms.<br /> <br /> What is your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T05:21:41-07:00","id":917295,"title":"","content":"I eventually learned to embrace pretty much everybody can do sorcery with a few exceptions, like vampires naturally translate it to their blood and soul point of view. But for instance allowing ghosts to learn sorcery all of a sudden secrets are awesome and the Library of Alexandria is a true treasure.<br /> <br /> but I view Arts and Realms as a type of magic tapping into a force of the Universe, magic of Archetypes channeled through Dreaming and whimsy. Sorcery seems to tap into inherent qualities like a form of practical physics that require will. I don't have a particular problem with them learning sorcery, its certainly one of the noggin crunching arguments. Like for instance Demons I would have they can't use sorcery because Lore is more a potent form of willful physics.<br /> <br /> I don't know its complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:02:41-07:00","id":917354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/917294-changelings-sorcery?p=917295#post917295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I eventually learned to embrace pretty much everybody can do sorcery with a few exceptions, like vampires naturally translate it to their blood and soul point of view. But for instance allowing ghosts to learn sorcery all of a sudden secrets are awesome and the Library of Alexandria is a true treasure.<br /> <br /> but I view Arts and Realms as a type of magic tapping into a force of the Universe, magic of Archetypes channeled through Dreaming and whimsy. Sorcery seems to tap into inherent qualities like a form of practical physics that require will. I don't have a particular problem with them learning sorcery, its certainly one of the noggin crunching arguments. Like for instance Demons I would have they can't use sorcery because Lore is more a potent form of willful physics.<br /> <br /> I don't know its complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think just like you. As paradigms are banal, dreaming the only true form of the magic. Since as time passes mage's are leave behind their paradigms (like support wheels), they start the use same kind of magic. However, I think after some point they do the magic without a channel like Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:49:33-07:00","id":917428,"title":"","content":"Games that I have played in are generally of the opinion that a full Changeling cannot learn sorcery, but a Kinain can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}